 "encoding": "For pixel p and band b: S = asinh(K*Lmean)/asinh(K*260) with K=0.97435, where Lmean is the area mean of the de-stretched linear 8-bit level L of every HiPS PNG pixel inside the order-6 pixel (L recovered by inverting the HipsGen asinh LUT g=floor(255*asinh(K*L)/asinh(K*260))). S is on the same 0..1 asinh scale as hipsRender.ts sampleSpectrum (value = g/254) but averaged in the linear domain. z = (S - median[b]) / sigma[b]; stored byte = round(clip(z,-4,4) * 127/4); -128 = no data. Decode: z = byte * 4/127; S ~= median[b] + z*sigma[b] (exact only inside the clip). For SHAPE matching subtract each pixel's mean z over valid bands (and normalise) before comparing, since a uniformly brighter pixel has positive z everywhere.",
