 "notes": [
  "Real SPHEREx DR1 data, but derived from the DISPLAY-STRETCHED 8-bit PNG HiPS tiles (asinh, cut 0..40 MJy/sr), not from calibrated images: values are a picture of the sky, good for comparing spectral SHAPES, not for photometry.",
  "The PNG grey values are an asinh LUT of an integer linear level (~0.157 MJy/sr per level if the 0..40 MJy/sr cut maps linearly onto 0..255 - an inference). Most high-latitude pixels are at level 0 in every band: the cube appears background (zodiacal light) subtracted and clipped at 0, so faint-sky spectra are mostly noise / quantisation.",
  "Frames 50 and 51 (band 3 ch 17, band 4 ch 1, dichroic channels) are blank in the cube (valid=false, stored -128).",
  "Order-6 pixels are ~0.92 deg across (49152 pixels, ~0.84 deg^2 each); every value is an area average over ~4096 order-12 HiPS pixels.",
